-- title:
--   The cusp-sum formula for `pair` holds for every primitive
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma$ be a subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of finite index, let $\varphi,\psi\colon \Gamma \to \mathbb{Q}$ be homomorphisms from the additivised group $\Gamma$ to $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $h\colon\Gamma\to\mathbb{Q}$ be any function satisfying the predicate [`ModularCurve.CupPairing.IsPrimitive`](def/ModularCurve_CupPairing.html#L10), i.e. $h(gg') = h(g)+h(g')-\omega(g,g')$ for all $g,g'\in\Gamma$, where $\omega(g,g')=\varphi(g)\psi(g')-\psi(g)\varphi(g')$. Then the rational number [`ModularCurve.CupPairing.pair`](def/ModularCurve_CupPairing.html#L18) $\Gamma\,\varphi\,\psi$ — defined, for $\Gamma$ of finite index admitting at least one such $h$, as the cusp sum of an arbitrarily chosen primitive divided by $2m_\Gamma$ — is equal to $\bigl(\sum_{q}h(\pi_q)\bigr)/(2m_\Gamma)$ for the given $h$. Here $q$ ranges over the (finitely many) orbits of the cyclic group generated by $T=\begin{pmatrix}1&1\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$ acting on $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})/\Gamma$, the element $\pi_q = x^{-1}T^{w}x\in\Gamma$ is [`ModularCurve.PDPairing.cuspGen`](def/ModularCurve_PDPairing.html#L570) attached to $q$ ($x$ a chosen representative of a chosen point $x\Gamma$ of the orbit, $w$ the minimal period of $T$ acting on that point), and $m_\Gamma = 1$ if $-1\in\Gamma$ and $m_\Gamma = 2$ otherwise.
--
--   This is the well-definedness statement underlying the cusp-residue (Shimura-type) formula for the antisymmetrised cup pairing of two rational characters of $\Gamma$: the quantity `pair`, defined through a chosen primitive of the $2$-cocycle $\omega$, may be computed from any primitive whatsoever. It is the form in which the cusp-sum formula is applied downstream, for instance in the construction of a perfect antisymmetric pairing on the corner submodule of $H^1$ and in the comparison of the pairing with Hecke, diamond and Fricke operators.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_CupPairing_pair_eq_cuspSum_div_of_isPrimitive.lean

